  {
    "id": "df2a1eb7-8647-5f50-9d73-d6b9fe033d16",
    "pack": "book-of-the-dead",
    "kind": "equipment",
    "slug": "equipment:soul-cage",
    "name": "Soul Cage",
    "level": 12,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["arcane", "void"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "book-of-the-dead"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As you Craft your "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "soul cage",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", you trap your soul within it, an integral part of the complicated process of becoming a lich. When you're destroyed, your soul flees to the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "soul cage",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", which rebuilds your undead body over the course of 1d10 days. Afterward, you manifest next to the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "soul cage",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", fully healed and in a new body (lacking any equipment you had on your old body). Only destroying your "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "soul cage",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " can prevent you from returning."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You choose the form of your "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "soul cage",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " when you Craft it. A few options include a miniature cage, a ring, an amulet, or a crown. Work with your GM to adjust the usage and Bulk as needed, though a soul cage is rarely more than light Bulk. The soul cage has Hardness 9 and 36 HP."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If your "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "soul cage",
            "marks": ["emphasis"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is destroyed but you aren't, you can attempt to find your soul and trap it again, building a new soul cage. This is no trivial feat and often takes an entire adventure to accomplish. If you don't cage your soul again, you suffer a long decline."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Craft Requirements",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You have Lich Dedication."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
